        "**Path integration** is the continual updating of direction and distance from a starting point using information gathered during movement. The **home vector** specifies the direction and distance back to the nest, so it summarizes the whole outward trip in one vector rather than retracing each turn. It is a computation that runs continuously, so the ant always holds an estimate of where the nest lies.",
        "Müller and Wehner recorded a natural foraging trip of Cataglyphis fortis in Tunisia. The outward path measured 354.5 m, while the maximum distance from the nest was 113.2 m. After finding food, the ant returned along a comparatively direct inbound route, so the homing path was far shorter than the outward path.",
